{
  "description": "T1 - Magnolia - reduce laterals\r8m in height.  No reduction to height.  Reduce laterals by 2m from 9m to 7m towards the house and over the southern neighbouring garden.  An established multi-stemmed magnolia in the rear garden, standing close to the side elevation of the house. Its lateral growth has extended towards the building and across the boundary over the neighbouring garden. The proposed reduction is confined to those two aspects and is the minimum intervention needed to restore clearance from the house and reduce the overhang, while retaining the tree's natural form and its amenity value in the garden.",
